{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-dreaming/1438349-the-higher-hunting-grounds","id":1438349,"title":"The Higher Hunting Grounds?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Changeling: The Dreaming"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-03-06T13:17:24-08:00","id":1438349,"title":"The Higher Hunting Grounds?","content":"Ok, so, the Higher Hunting Grounds were the Nunnehi equivalent of Arcadia, and, during the Shattering, it was either destroyed or lost forever. As a result, Nunnehi are 'cut off' from the Deeaming to a very large extent, filling the Umbra in the Dreaming's place. That said, I have a few questions.<br /> <br /> 1.Can Nunnehi use/open trods?<br /> 2.What stops s Nunnehi from using Oneiromancy \u2022\u2022\u2022 to open an artificial trod?<br /> 3.They still patently interact with chimerical reality, right?<br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-06T13:47:31-08:00","id":1438352,"title":"","content":"And what do you think their version of the Tuatha de Danaan were? I don't mean in a Kithain sense, but rather &quot;godlike progenitors now long lost&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-06T15:05:59-08:00","id":1438369,"title":"","content":"Nunnehi can still go into the Dreaming they are just synched with the Umbra and Dark Umbra, Oneiromancy I believe works normal for them. They do interact with Chimerical Reality.<br /> <br /> I reckon their Tuatha and Fomorians were the great spirits and beasts of Legend from different Cultures. Some might actually be in the Umbra now... maybe maybe not. I can see the Great Mystery Wakan Tankan for instance being revered, and their totems seem to be more tied to plants and landscape features rather then Animals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-07T05:32:33-08:00","id":1438456,"title":"","content":"At least some Native American deities would have aspects of themselves in the dreaming. Coyote, Raven, and Rabbit, strike me as most likely. But White Buffalo Woman and Trap Door Spider Woman seem right too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 03-07-2021, 03:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-07T11:07:08-08:00","id":1438478,"title":"","content":"Coyote sing the Universe into being seems sublimely Dreaming.<br /> <br /> And maybe the Umbral Totems of the Nunnehi exist in both Worlds, so Maize Woman could be a Fae being.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-07T11:12:27-08:00","id":1438479,"title":"","content":"No reason why statless gods can\u2019t have multiple incarnations throughout the Otherworlds. I imagine something like Maize Woman isn\u2019t even a full being, rather is an Incarna avatar of Gaia. <br /> <br /> Dana, Mother of the Tuatha de Danaan, is a Middle Umbral spirit. Yet she spawned a race of Dreaming gods who do <i>not</i> inhabit <i>any</i> Otherworlds than their own.<br /> <br /> Which is why in my games, quite a few Gaian and Wyld Incarna have Green Roads of Balor in their Umbral demesnes, most notably Dana and Stag.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-28T23:20:27-07:00","id":1453743,"title":"","content":"European changelings broke the Nunnehi's &quot;sideways trods&quot;' via trail-razing in the 15th century, severing their connections to the High Hunting Grounds. It's in Dreams and Nightmares.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/m